[INFO] 09-22 20:37:00 run_experiments.py:74] 开始处理问题： In quantum mechanics, when calculating the interaction between the electron with the proton in a hydrogen atom, it is necessary to compute the following volume integral (over all space):
[INFO] 09-22 20:37:00 run_experiments.py:74] $$
[INFO] 09-22 20:37:00 run_experiments.py:74] \mathbf{I}=\int \mathbf{B}(\mathbf{r})|\Psi(\mathbf{r})|^{2} d V
[INFO] 09-22 20:37:00 run_experiments.py:74] $$
[INFO] 09-22 20:37:00 run_experiments.py:74] 
[INFO] 09-22 20:37:00 run_experiments.py:74] where $\Psi(\mathbf{r})$ is the spatial wavefunction of the electron as a function of position $\mathbf{r}$ and $\mathbf{B}(\mathbf{r})$ is the (boldface denotes vector) magnetic field produced by the proton at position $\mathbf{r}$. Suppose the proton is located at the origin and it acts like a finite-sized magnetic dipole (but much smaller than $a_{0}$ ) with dipole moment
[INFO] 09-22 20:37:00 run_experiments.py:74] 
[INFO] 09-22 20:37:00 run_experiments.py:74] $\mu_{p}=1.41 \times 10^{-26} \mathrm{~J} / \mathrm{T}$. Let the hydrogen atom be in the ground state, meaning $\Psi(\mathbf{r})=\frac{e^{-r / a_{0}}}{\sqrt{\pi a_{0}^{3}}}$, where $a_{0}=5.29 \times 10^{-11} \mathrm{~m}$ is the Bohr radius. Evaluate the magnitude of the integral $|\mathbf{I}|$ (in SI units).
