[INFO] 09-22 23:18:11 run_experiments.py:74] 2. Partitioning participants into disjoint sets (A: initially promoted, B: 60 ≤ original score < 65, C: original score < 60)  
[INFO] 09-22 23:18:11 run_experiments.py:74] 3. Relating pre- and post-increase averages via score adjustments (adding 5 to all scores)  
[INFO] 09-22 23:18:11 run_experiments.py:74] 4. Solving Diophantine equations derived from average constraints (e.g., 71P + 56R = 66N for initial totals).  
