[INFO] 09-22 23:18:11 run_experiments.py:74] 
[INFO] 09-22 23:18:11 run_experiments.py:74] **Pitfall Prediction**: 
[INFO] 09-22 23:18:11 run_experiments.py:74] - *Conceptual Trap*: Assuming the triangle is entirely within the square, which would incorrectly use the full triangle area ($ \frac{1}{2} \times 10 \times h = 80 \implies h = 16 $), but this ignores that $ h = 16 $ places $ G $ at $ y = -6 $, making part of the triangle outside the square (below $ y = 0 $).
[INFO] 09-22 23:18:11 run_experiments.py:74] - *Calculation Trap*: Sign errors in line equations (e.g., miscalculating slopes for EG/MG) or miscomputing the bottom base length as $ \frac{100}{h} $ instead of $ 10 - \frac{100}{h} $.
[INFO] 09-22 23:18:11 run_experiments.py:74] - *Completeness Trap*: Failing to recognize the trapezoid shape of the intersection region and using the wrong area formula (e.g., triangle area instead of trapezoid).
