[INFO] 09-22 23:18:11 run_experiments.py:74] **Core Principle Identification**: The core principle involves the structure of subgroups of $\mathbb{Z}^2$, specifically using integer linear algebra to determine the congruence conditions defining the subgroup $H$. For $H = H_{xy}$, elements of $H_{xy}$ must satisfy $b \equiv y a \pmod{x}$ for $(a, b) \in H_{xy}$. To find $x$ and $y$, we compute the greatest common divisor (gcd) of the 2x2 minors of the generator matrix and derive the congruence relation from the linear dependencies among the generators.
[INFO] 09-22 23:18:11 run_experiments.py:74] 
[INFO] 09-22 23:18:11 run_experiments.py:74] **Pitfall Prediction**: 
