[INFO] 09-22 23:18:11 run_experiments.py:74] **Core Principle Identification**: The mean molecular speed in an ideal gas is derived from the Maxwell-Boltzmann distribution and requires the formula $ v = \sqrt{\frac{8RT}{\pi M}} $, where $ R = 8.314 \, \text{J/(mol·K)} $ (gas constant), $ T $ is temperature in Kelvin, and $ M $ is the molar mass in **kg/mol**. For hydrogen gas (H₂), the molar mass must account for its diatomic nature (2 × atomic mass of hydrogen).  
[INFO] 09-22 23:18:11 run_experiments.py:74] **Pitfall Prediction**:  
[INFO] 09-22 23:18:11 run_experiments.py:74] - *Conceptual Traps*: Using molar mass in **g/mol** (e.g., 2.016 g/mol) instead of **kg/mol** (0.002016 kg/mol), which would produce a result **31.6× too small** (since $ \sqrt{1000} \approx 31.6 $). Confusing mean speed with root-mean-square speed (which uses $ \sqrt{3RT/M} $).  
[INFO] 09-22 23:18:11 run_experiments.py:74] - *Calculation Traps*: Assuming an incorrect standard temperature (e.g., 298 K instead of 273 K for STP), or omitting unit conversions (e.g., failing to convert g/mol to kg/mol).  
[INFO] 09-22 23:18:11 run_experiments.py:74] - *Completeness Traps*: Stopping after deriving the formula without computing the final numerical value, or neglecting the diatomic nature of H₂ (using atomic hydrogen mass instead of molecular).  
[INFO] 09-22 23:18:11 run_experiments.py:74] **Strategy Formulation**:  
[INFO] 09-22 23:18:11 run_experiments.py:74] 1. Assume **standard temperature $ T = 273 \, \text{K} $** (0°C), as it is conventional for gas speed calculations when unspecified.  
[INFO] 09-22 23:18:11 run_experiments.py:74] 2. Calculate the molar mass of H₂: atomic hydrogen mass is $ 1.008 \, \text{g/mol} $, so H₂ is $ 2.016 \, \text{g/mol} $. Convert to **kg/mol** ($ 0.002016 \, \text{kg/mol} $).  
[INFO] 09-22 23:18:11 run_experiments.py:74] 3. Apply the exact formula $ v = \sqrt{\frac{8 \cdot R \cdot T}{\pi \cdot M}} $ with $ R = 8.314 \, \text{J/(mol·K)} $, substituting $ T $ and $ M $ from Steps 1–2.  
[INFO] 09-22 23:18:11 run_experiments.py:74] 4. Compute the numerical result in **m/s**, ensuring all units cancel correctly to yield velocity.
[INFO] 09-22 23:18:11 run_experiments.py:74] </think>
