[INFO] 09-22 23:18:11 run_experiments.py:74]  number $a(r, c)$ in the cell in row $r$ and column $c$. A pair $(R, C)$, where $R$ is a set of rows and $C$ a set of columns, is called a saddle pair if the following two conditions are satisfied:(i) For each row $r^{\prime}$, there is $r \in R$ such that $a(r, c) \geqslant a\left(r^{\prime}, c\right)$ for all $c \in C$;
[INFO] 09-22 23:18:11 run_experiments.py:74] 
[INFO] 09-22 23:18:11 run_experiments.py:74] (ii) For each column $c^{\prime}$, there is $c \in C$ such that $a(r, c) \leqslant a\left(r, c^{\prime}\right)$ for all $r \in R$.
[INFO] 09-22 23:18:11 run_experiments.py:74] 
[INFO] 09-22 23:18:11 run_experiments.py:74] A saddle pair $(R, C)$ is called a minimal pair if for each saddle pair $\left(R^{\prime}, C^{\prime}\right)$ with $R^{\prime} \subseteq R$ and $C^{\prime} \subseteq C$, we have $R^{\prime}=R$ and $C^{\prime}=C$.
[INFO] 09-22 23:18:11 run_experiments.py:74] 
[INFO] 09-22 23:18:11 run_experiments.py:74] Prove that any two minimal pairs contain the same number of rows.
